SUMMARY:FirstWord: Medical Affairs in 2027: Proving the value we create for
  patients
DESCRIPTION:Medical affairs has always advanced patient outcomes. What has 
 been harder is capturing that contribution in the language the enterprise 
 measures by. Most organizations still track the function through engagemen
 ts held\, insights captured and evidence generated\, because these are the
  measures the field matured around. The more revealing question\, and the 
 one medical affairs leaders are increasingly asking themselves\, is what s
 hifted as a result of that work. This webinar examines what it would take 
 for medical affairs in 2027 to make that contribution visible more directl
 y.\n\nThe discussion will explore how organizations can develop richer mea
 sures of impact\, work through the genuine difficulty of attribution\, and
  complement activity metrics with outcome-oriented ones. It will also cons
 ider how agentic AI and the right intelligence infrastructure can help med
 ical affairs connect priorities\nType: FW Perspectives Live\nSponsor: ZS A
 ssociates\nSpeakers: Jimmy Baudot\, Associate Principal\, ZS Associates\; 
 Rico Calara\, PhD\, Director Medical Insights\, Digital\, & Analytics Stra
 tegy\, argenx\; and Leela Barham\, Moderator\, FirstWord\nRegister Now: ht
 tps://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/4517900878184/WN_aqgztAZSQvGMDKUUhQ
 Bg5Q\nSource: https://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/4517900878184/WN_aq
 gztAZSQvGMDKUUhQBg5Q
URL:https://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/4517900878184/WN_aqgztAZSQvGMD
 KUUhQBg5Q
